---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { demoCallsData } from '../lib/demo-calls.mjs';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/stories.mjs';
const demo = demoCallsData();
const title = 'About & how we rank';
const description = 'aiphonecompare is the independent, verified price comparison for AI receptionists: every price sourced and dated, sponsored spots labeled, rankings not for sale.';
const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: title,
  url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href,
  description,
  isPartOf: { '@id': new URL('/#website', Astro.site).href },
  about: { '@id': new URL('/#organization', Astro.site).href },
};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} jsonld={jsonld}>
  <article class="wrap prose page-intro">
    <h1>How this site works</h1>
    <p class="lead">aiphonecompare is a free, independent site that compares AI phone answering services (also called AI receptionists) for small businesses, with real prices from each company's own website.</p>
    <h2 id="how-we-make-money">How we make money</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Free for businesses.</strong> Comparing, the cost tools and the price check cost you nothing.</li>
      <li><strong>Referral fees.</strong> Some links pay us a fee if you sign up. Each one is marked, and it never changes your price.</li>
      <li><strong>Labeled ad spots.</strong> Companies that sell AI phone answering can pay to show first on one industry page. It always says Sponsored.</li>
      <li><strong>Paid services.</strong> We offer a <a href="/done-for-you/">done-for-you setup</a> for businesses, and a <a href="/competitor-check-up/">competitor check-up</a> for the companies we list.</li>
      <li><strong>Rankings are not for sale.</strong> None of the above changes a price, a fact or the order of the lists.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Independent</h2>
    <p>No company we list owns us. Lists are in A to Z order, and we don't score companies yet. Sponsored listings may appear first and always carry a <span class="badge">Sponsored</span> label. Rankings are not for sale, and payment never changes a vendor's data.</p>
    <p>Some outbound links are referral links: we may earn a fee if you sign up, and each one is marked where it appears. Referral links never affect rankings, listings, verified prices, or the order of results. <a href="/terms/#referral">Referral links in our terms</a>.</p>
    <h2>Verified</h2>
    <p>Every price comes from the vendor's own website or a cited source, shown on the vendor's page with the date we last checked it. If we can't verify something, we leave it blank. We never guess prices.</p>
    <h2>By industry</h2>
    <p>Dental practices, law firms, plumbers, and medical practices need different things, like booking straight into dental software, patient privacy (HIPAA) paperwork, taking new-client details for a law firm, or sending after-hours emergencies to the right person. Each industry page compares only the tools that serve it, with a short buying guide. Phone-recording statutes are on the <a href="/call-recording-consent-by-state/">call recording consent</a> page.</p>
    <h2 id="demo-line-tests">How we test demo lines</h2>
    <p>On <time datetime={demo.method.date}>{formatDate(demo.method.date)}</time>, {demo.method.window}, {demo.method.placedBy} called {demo.calls.length} vendors' public demo lines. Each call checked four things in one conversation: {demo.method.tested.slice(0, -1).join(', ')}, and {demo.method.tested.at(-1)}. We did not test {demo.method.notTested.join('; ')}.</p>
    <p>{demo.method.note} Write-ups are on each company's page: {demo.calls.map((c, i) => <><a href={`/vendors/${c.slug}/#we-called-them`}>{c.name}</a>{i < demo.calls.length - 1 ? (i === demo.calls.length - 2 ? ' and ' : ', ') : ''}</>)}.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Vendors can ask us to confirm or correct their listing. We update it once we can verify the change against a public source.</p>
    <h2>For vendors</h2>
    <p>Listed vendors can add a free <a href="/badge/">"Listed on aiphonecompare" badge</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
